# Exercise Authoring

## When creating modules

- Scaffold TODO shells; never completed implementations.
- No `Solution.tsx` or `solution/` unless explicitly requested after the learner finishes.
- One main concept per module; ~30–60 minutes to complete.
- Reuse prior completed modules; do not introduce later concepts prematurely.
- Realistic data and browser-visible behavior where relevant.

## Module files (when appropriate)

```text
README.md
Warmup.ts
Exercise.tsx
Challenge.tsx
type-tests.ts
```

## TODO design

- Require type-design decisions, not syntax fill-in-the-blank.
- Include valid usage examples and invalid examples that must fail.
- Include positive type tests and negative tests with `@ts-expect-error`.

## README must include

Why it matters, problem solved, concept summary, small examples, common mistakes, exercise instructions, acceptance criteria, production relevance, reflection questions, official doc links — **no final solution**.

## Production challenge

Each module includes one production-style challenge with acceptance criteria and reflection questions.

## Sequential delivery

Only fully prepare the current unlocked module. Later modules may have placeholder READMEs only.
